(D8 — Discrepancy 8 repro: `is equal to` on two collections compiles and
 always answers "not equal", with no diagnostic — including two lists built
 from the identical literal, and a list compared against its own documented
 rendering as a text.
 LANGUAGE.md:1836-1842 and 4441-4443 present `is equal to` with no type
 restriction, and things ARE documented as compared field by field, so a
 reader has no warning that collections are the exception.
 This is what makes every whole-collection assertion in this ledger
 unavailable: `If xs is not equal to "[1, 2, 3]" then, Exit 95.` compiles
 and fires on EVERY run. The only oracle for a collection is per-element /
 per-key reads plus `length` / `empty`.
 Found while checking the `assertable?` column for LST-01; the claim lines
 are in the EXP ledger's range (1789-2025), not this one.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D8.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   identical lists: NOT equal
   identical maps: NOT equal
   list against its own rendering: NOT equal
   element-wise: ok
)
a list called lhs is [1, 2, 3].
a list called rhs is [1, 2, 3].
If lhs is equal to rhs then, print "identical lists: equal". Otherwise, print "identical lists: NOT equal".
a map called mapone is {"k": 1}.
a map called maptwo is {"k": 1}.
If mapone is equal to maptwo then, print "identical maps: equal". Otherwise, print "identical maps: NOT equal".
If lhs is equal to "[1, 2, 3]" then, print "list against its own rendering: equal". Otherwise, print "list against its own rendering: NOT equal".
If element 1 of lhs is equal to 1 and lhs's length is equal to 3 then, print "element-wise: ok". Otherwise, print "element-wise: BAD".
